# Sainted One — one of the five Guildlords of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 11/12 The Guildlords — 35 to 45 life, can't be bribed
# enemy: Sainted One (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0021.dck "Sainted One (Wh, 4th Edition)" [Tier 3 —
#   Manalink 3 file dated 2016-02-15; its first 17 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 20
#   lines (60 cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/sainted_one.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 11)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/sainted_one.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Guildlords) — "Sainted One"
#   (Original) [Tier-web — DIFFERS: main +{} -{}; side +{'Disenchant': 1} -{}]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Sainted One
22 Plains
1 Mox Pearl
1 Sol Ring
1 Black Lotus
1 Mishra's Workshop
2 White Mana Battery
2 Serra Angel
2 Personal Incarnation
3 White Knight
3 Rainbow Knights
2 Blessing
1 Balance
3 Dingus Egg
4 Circle of Protection: Artifacts
3 Armageddon Clock
3 Bottle of Suleiman
3 Armageddon
2 Swords to Plowshares
1 Disenchant
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   2 Swords to Plowshares, 1 Disenchant
#   .vBlack  1 Karma, 1 Circle of Protection: Black, 1 Angry Mob
#   .vBlue   2 Circle of Protection: Blue, 1 Disenchant
#   .vGreen  2 Circle of Protection: Green, 1 Disenchant
#   .vRed    2 Circle of Protection: Red, 1 Conversion
#   .vWhite  3 Circle of Protection: White, 2 Disenchant
# (the wiki lists the sideboard as 1 Angry Mob, 1 Circle of Protection: Black, 2 Circle of Protection: Blue, 2 Circle of Protection: Green, 2 Circle of Protection: Red, 3 Circle of Protection: White, 1 Conversion, 2 Disenchant, 1 Karma — same sections, a different fold)
SB: 1 Karma
SB: 1 Circle of Protection: Black
SB: 1 Angry Mob
SB: 2 Circle of Protection: Blue
SB: 1 Disenchant
SB: 2 Circle of Protection: Green
SB: 2 Circle of Protection: Red
SB: 1 Conversion
SB: 3 Circle of Protection: White
